##gff-version 3
# Faba bean necrotic yellows virus (FBNYV), isolate EV1-93 (Egypt): eight
# circular ssDNA components of about 1 kb (genus Nanovirus), in the order of
# ICTV 9th Report Nanoviridae Fig. 2:
#   DNA-R NC_003560.1  DNA-S NC_003563.1  DNA-C NC_003559.1  DNA-M NC_003562.1
#   DNA-N NC_003566.1  DNA-U1 NC_003561.1 DNA-U2 NC_003564.1 DNA-U4 NC_024457.1
# Coordinates are those of the RefSeq records, each of which starts at the
# common-region stem-loop (RefSeq's stem_loop 1..29 / 1..33 rows are kept,
# so the hairpin icon sits on it), so it sits at 12 o'clock as in the figure.
# RefSeq's TATA_box / polyA_signal_sequence rows are omitted (VirPlot would
# ignore them anyway). Products
# are the figure's names (M-Rep, CP, Clink, MP, NSP, U1, U2, U4). For DNA-U4,
# RefSeq also gives a short variant (445..693) of the same ORF; only the full
# ORF is kept.
